  "Analysis": [
    {
      "predicate": "iadas:typeOfAnalysis",
      "object": "Correlation"
    },
    {
      "predicate": "iadas:authorConclusion",
      "object": "Social pressure, social support, self esteem, body dissatisfaction was related to DE. Social support was not strongly related to DE.. Activity specific body image dissatisfaction is a better predictor of DE than general body image dissatisfaction. When the pressure to be thin was introduced into the model, the competitive level was no longer significant in predicting aesthetic performers DE. Our final model explained 61% of the variance in aesthetic performers disordered eating and also confirmed the role of low self esteem and specific body image dissatisfaction as partial mediators from pressure to be thin to DE."
    },
    {
      "predicate": "iadas:limites",
      "object": "Small size of the groups of male aesthetic performers, and the absence of a group of non elite male ballet dancers. The cross sectional design does not allow for full comprehension of the relationship between participation in these activities and the development of disordered eating. The use of self-report questionnaires and the fact that we have not taken into account the percentage of respondents and non respondents."
    },
    {
      "predicate": "iadas:perspectives",
      "object": "It is important to distinguish between pressure on Female and male aesthetic performers. Such preventative measures are essential in professional dancer schools and especially gymnastics clubs. These actions should focus on promoting young aesthetic performer's self-esteem and satisfaction with their activity specific body image, which is essential to reducing the impact of pressure to be thin on their eating and weight control behaviors. Coaches and teachers sould understand the impact of their behaviors and comments that lead aesthetic performers to adopt unhealthy practices and should try to adjust their demands to healthier ideal body requirements for the practice of classical dance or gymnastics."
    },
